hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15477","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar ibn Hawshab narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: They had a slave boy called Tahman or Dhakwan, so his grandfather freed half of him. So the slave came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are freed in your freedom and enslaved in your bondage. He said: And he served his master until he died. Abd al-Razzaq said: And Mamar, meaning Ibn Hawshab, was a righteous man."
"15478","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Amir ibn Salih ibn Rustum al-Muzani informed us, Ayyub ibn Musa ibn Amr ibn Said ibn al-Asi, he said: or Ibn Said ibn al-As, narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No father grants his child better than good upbringing."
"15479","Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Khalaf ibn Hisham al-Bazzar and al-Qawariri narrated it to us, both said: Amir ibn Abi Amir narrated to us with its isnad, and he mentioned the like of it."
